From fd02fe65e9d2fd6f658dfd9221232ad6542d0e2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 06:00:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Voxel engine: 384-high world, subchunks, flood-fill lighting,
 border-aware meshing

- World height -64..319 (Minecraft 1.18+), columns split into 24 16x16x16 subchunks
  with per-subchunk meshes/colliders; only touched subchunks rebuild
- Minecraft flood-fill lighting: separate sky + block light (0-15), BFS add/remove,
  sky light falls at full strength, floods across chunk borders, incremental updates on edit
- Smooth per-vertex light + AO in the mesher; sky/block light are separate attributes so the
  day/night cycle dims sky light in the shader without remeshing
- Meshing uses an 18^3 padded copy including neighbour chunks; chunks are only meshed once all
  8 neighbours exist and are lit, so border faces are culled correctly
- Atlas tiles now have edge-extruded gutters (and Steve's skin UVs are inset) to remove seams
- Glowstone block (emits light 15), glowing cave ceilings, mountains and caves in terrain
- Budgeted streaming (terrain -> light -> mesh), batched explosions, edited chunks are kept
